## Required:
Previously, you've installed boot9strap, a custom firmware loader that loads the file boot.firm from SD card or NAND (internal memory).
We are using Luma3DS by LumaTeam as our boot.firm to patch the console, allowing it to run homebrew software.

Here, we will make critical system file backups and install some homebrew programs. Most of these steps are automated using a script that is ran from the console.

The script will install the following applications:
# FBI 
by Steveice10 (installs CIA formatted applications)
# Homebrew Launcher Loader
by PabloMK7 (runs Homebrew Launcher for 3DSX format)
# Anemone3DS
by astronautlevel2 (installs custom themes, splashes, and badges)
# Checkpoint
by BernardoGiordano/FlagBrew (manages 3DS/DS game save data)
# ftpd
by mtheall (allows wireless 3DS SD card access over FTP)
# Universal Updater
by Universal-Team (on device app store for downloading homebrew over Wi-Fi)
# GodMode9
by d0k3 (multipurpose tool for extracting data from internal memory or cartridges)

If you dont want these applications, you can remove them after you have finished this process byt navigating to
System Settings > Data Management > Nintendo 3DS > Software (exception of GodMode9)



## What you need:
x_finalize_helper.firm
finalize.romfs



## Instructions
# Section I | Prep Work
In this section you will copy ther necessary files to follow the rest of the instructions

1. Power off your console
2. Insert SD into computer
3. Copy finalize.romfs to root of the SD card
4. Open the luma folder on SD card, if a folder named "payloads" is not present, create one
5. Copy x_finalize_helper.firm to the payloads folder
6. Reinster SD to console


# Section II | Updating the System
Here you will update the system to the latest version, which is safe to do with custom firmware
1. Navigate to System Settings > Other Settings > System Update
- Updates while using B9S + Luma are safe
- Updater may display message, "Your system is up to date" in which case move onto the next section
- If this gives you an error, set your DNS settings to "Auto" and Proxy settings to "No"
- If you still receive an error, visit the troubleshooting guide


